WebdriverIO (8 and 9) helper for this template — in a WebdriverIO suite, use it as written:
Facts:
  • hidden radio inputs, operated by their labels — click the label, assert the input
  • the inputs carry the option name in aria-label and a value ("teams" / "individuals") in name="plan_type_selector"
  • assert the input's selected state, not that it exists (it is hidden)
```js
const planTypeInput = (option) => $(`input[name="plan_type_selector"][aria-label="${option}"]`);

// The radios are hidden: click the visible label, then wait for the input to be selected.
async function selectPlanType(option) {
  const input = planTypeInput(option);
  if (!(await input.isExisting())) throw new Error(`No plan type "${option}" on the page`);
  await $(`label[for="${await input.getAttribute('id')}"]`).click();
  await browser.waitUntil(() => input.isSelected(), { timeoutMsg: `Plan type "${option}" was not selected after clicking its label` });
}
```
